(6678404, 999077, 49018, '<td valign="top">I find it interesting in many respects.<br/>You have put together to kind of processing that belongs to two different eras, really. The sharpness of the eye and still the extremely soft PP, reminiscent of other times.<br/>I find the image enigmatic, in a sense. Are the flowers the gentle back of dad''s hand, to grab and  squeeze tight against the cheek? (My kid does that a lot, it comforts him).<br/>I have been looking at this since a while now.<br/>So, well, a revisitable 9.</td>', 'I find it interesting in many respects.You have put together to kind of processing that belongs to two different eras, really. The sharpness of the eye and still the extremely soft PP, reminiscent of other times.I find the image enigmatic, in a sense. Are the flowers the gentle back of dad''s hand, to grab and  squeeze tight against the cheek? (My kid does that a lot, it comforts him).I have been looking at this since a while now.So, well, a revisitable 9.', '2012-02-15 19:06:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6678405, 998941, 49018, '<td valign="top">Funny idea.</td>', 'Funny idea.', '2012-02-15 19:06:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6678413, 999075, 49018, '<td valign="top">If I understand the intent, a different lighting showing off the glass reflections and transparency, possibly a less opaque type of glass and a perfect reflection, would have turned this into a very high scoring image.<br/>This way probably not.<br/>Along with many very good instructionals online , many say this book is the bible of tricky materials studio photography:<i> Light: Science and Magic: An Introduction to Photographic Lighting</i>, if that can help.<br/> <br/>Unless I completely missed your intent and the above remarks are well meant but completely irrelevant, of course.</td>', 'If I understand the intent, a different lighting showing off the glass reflections and transparency, possibly a less opaque type of glass and a perfect reflection, would have turned this into a very high scoring image.This way probably not.Along with many very good instructionals online , many say this book is the bible of tricky materials studio photography: Light: Science and Magic: An Introduction to Photographic Lighting, if that can help. Unless I completely missed your intent and the above remarks are well meant but completely irrelevant, of course.', '2012-02-15 19:13:48.000000', NULL, 1),
